= Masail e Hajj --- Class 6 Summary
<masail-e-hajj-class-6-summary>
#class-meta(
  date: [May 21, 2026],
  topic: [Arkān of Hajj: Wuqūf Arafah --- its obligation, place, timing, and related rulings],
  teacher: [Mufti Umar Aejaz],
)


== Introduction
<introduction>
This class begins the study of the #strong[Arkān (أَرْكَان)] \[pillars\] of
Hajj --- the mandatory actions without which Hajj is not performed at
all. The two arkān are:

+ #strong[Wuqūf Arafah (وُقُوفُ عَرَفَة)] --- standing at the plain of Arafah.
+ #strong[Ṭawāf al-Ziyārah (طَوَافُ الزِّيَارَة)] --- details to follow in a
  future class.

This session focuses entirely on Wuqūf Arafah, covering six key points:

+ The #strong[dalīl] (evidence) behind its obligation
+ The #strong[place] where it is performed
+ The #strong[time] in which it is performed
+ The #strong[duration] of the stay
+ Rulings related to the wuqūf
+ What happens if someone #strong[misses] the wuqūf

#horizontalrule

== Point 1 --- The Dalīl (Evidence) for the Farḍiyyah of Wuqūf Arafah
<point-1-the-dalil-evidence-for-the-far-iyyah-of-wuquf-arafah>
Allah obligated Hajj in the Quran in a #strong[mujmal (مُجْمَل)]
\[general\] manner --- without specifying its details. The details were
provided by the Prophet ﷺ through aḥādīth. He explained what the essence
of Hajj is:

=== Ḥadīth 1
<hadith-1>
#quote(block: true)[
اَلْحَجُّ عَرَفَةُ

#emph["Hajj is Arafah."]

#strong[(hadith as cited in class --- confirm in hadith index)]
]

The meaning is: #emph[the Hajj is \[essentially\] the standing at
Arafah.] The Prophet ﷺ based the completion of Hajj upon this single
action, indicating that it is the #strong[farḍ] \[obligatory pillar\]
without which Hajj does not exist at all.

=== The Nature of "Completion" (Tamām) Here
<the-nature-of-completion-tamam-here>
A question arises: when the completion of something depends on an
action, that action should be #strong[wājib];, not farḍ --- because a
wājib is what completes an already-existing thing. The answer is that
#strong[completion (tamām)] is of two types:

+ #strong[Completion in the sense of existence (wujūd):] The thing does
  not exist at all without the action.
+ #strong[Completion in the sense of perfection (kamāl):] The thing
  exists but remains incomplete.

Here, the first meaning is intended. The ḥadīth means: whoever performs
the wuqūf at Arafah, his Hajj #strong[comes into existence];. Without
it, the Hajj has no existence whatsoever. Since the Quranic āyah
obligating Hajj is at the level of #strong[farḍ];, and this ḥadīth is
its tafsīr, the wuqūf too is established as farḍ --- not merely wājib.

#horizontalrule

=== Ḥadīth 2 / Āyah of Quran
<hadith-2-ayah-of-quran>
#quote(block: true)[
ثُمَّ أَفِيضُوا مِنْ حَيْثُ أَفَاضَ النَّاسُ

#emph["Then return from where the people return from."]

#strong[Ref:] Sūrah al-Baqarah (2:199)
]

=== Background
<background>
During the Jāhiliyyah period, the people of Makkah (the people of the
Ḥaram) would #strong[not go to Arafah] during Hajj. They would say:
#emph["We are the people of Allah's Ḥaram; we will not leave its
boundaries like others."] Since Arafah is located #strong[outside] the
boundary of the Ḥaram, they would remain within it and skip the wuqūf.

This āyah was revealed commanding them to return from where other people
return from --- i.e., from Arafah. The command to return from Arafah
implicitly requires going there in the first place. Thus, indirectly,
this is an order to perform the wuqūf.

=== Dalīl 3 --- Ijmāʿ (Consensus)
<dalil-3-ijma-consensus>
There is #strong[ijmāʿ] (consensus) among all the scholars and schools
of thought that Wuqūf Arafah is farḍ. No difference of opinion exists on
this point.

#horizontalrule

== Point 2 --- The Place of Wuqūf
<point-2-the-place-of-wuquf>
The entire plain of Arafah is the place for the wuqūf, as stated by the
Prophet ﷺ:

#quote(block: true)[
وَقَفْتُ هَاهُنَا وَعَرَفَةُ كُلُّهَا مَوْقِفٌ

#emph["I stood here, and the whole of Arafah is a place of standing."]

#strong[(hadith as cited in class --- confirm in hadith index)]
]

The Prophet ﷺ mentioned the wuqūf in #strong[absolute terms] without
restricting it to any particular spot. Therefore, one may stand anywhere
in the field of Arafah.

=== Exception: Baṭn ʿUranah (بَطْنُ عُرَنَة)
<exception-ba-n-uranah>
The only exception is the #strong[Valley of ʿUranah];, a specific strip
of land within the area. The Prophet ﷺ prohibited standing there for
wuqūf and called it a #strong["mawqif of Shayṭān"] --- because Shayṭān
would love for people to stand there, as their wuqūf would not be valid.
Apart from this valley, the entire field is permissible.

#horizontalrule

== Point 3 --- The Time of Wuqūf
<point-3-the-time-of-wuquf>
The time for Wuqūf Arafah is fixed as follows:

- #strong[Beginning:] After the #strong[zawāl] (when the sun passes its
  zenith and Ẓuhr time begins) on the #strong[9th of Dhul Ḥijjah] (Yawm
  al-ʿArafah).
- #strong[End:] Before the #strong[Fajr time] begins on the #strong[10th
  of Dhul Ḥijjah] (Yawm al-Naḥr).

This gives a window of less than twenty-four hours. Any stay at Arafah
outside this window is #strong[not counted] as wuqūf --- similar to how
a ṣalāh cannot be performed before its prescribed time.

=== Evidence for the Beginning
<evidence-for-the-beginning>
#quote(block: true)[
خُذُوا عَنِّي مَنَاسِكَكُمْ

#emph["Learn from me your rites of Hajj."]

#strong[(hadith as cited in class --- confirm in hadith index)]
]

The Prophet ﷺ performed the wuqūf after the zawāl, and instructed the
Ummah to learn their Hajj from his practice. This establishes the zawāl
as the starting point.

=== Evidence for the End
<evidence-for-the-end>
#quote(block: true)[
مَنْ أَدْرَكَ عَرَفَةَ بِلَيْلٍ فَقَدْ أَدْرَكَ الْحَجَّ ، وَمَنْ فَاتَهُ عَرَفَةُ بِلَيْلٍ فَقَدْ فَاتَهُ الْحَجُّ

#emph["Whoever reaches Arafah at night has attained the Hajj; and
whoever misses Arafah at night has missed the Hajj."]

#strong[(hadith as cited in class --- confirm in hadith index)]
]

#horizontalrule

=== Difference of Opinion: Day vs.~Night
<difference-of-opinion-day-vs-night>
#figure(
  align(center)[#table(
    columns: (47.37%, 52.63%),
    align: (auto,auto,),
    table.header([Scholar], [Position],),
    table.hline(),
    [#strong[Aḥnāf (Ḥanafī school)] --- Majority view], [The time for
    wuqūf includes #strong[both day and night];. One may perform it at
    any point after the zawāl on the 9th until Fajr of the 10th.],
    [#strong[Imām Mālik];], [The actual time for wuqūf is only the
    #strong[night portion];. If someone was present only during the
    daytime and left before night, their wuqūf is #strong[not valid];.],
  )]
  , kind: table
  )

#strong[Imām Mālik's Dalīl:] He relies on the ḥadīth: #emph["Whoever
reaches Arafah at night has attained the Hajj."] Since the ḥadīth
restricts attainment to the night, Imām Mālik restricts the wuqūf to the
night.

#strong[Ḥanafī Response:]

#quote(block: true)[
مَنْ وَقَفَ بِعَرَفَةَ بِلَيْلٍ أَوْ نَهَارٍ فَقَدْ تَمَّ حَجُّهُ

#emph["Whoever stood at Arafah --- whether by night or by day --- his
Hajj is complete."]

#strong[(hadith as cited in class --- confirm in hadith index)]
]

This explicitly includes the #strong[daytime] as a valid period. Both
day and night are options; neither is exclusive.

#strong[Additional Reasoning:] Wuqūf Arafah is one of the actions of
Hajj, and other actions of Hajj are not restricted to nighttime alone.
By analogy, the wuqūf should likewise not be restricted to the night.

#strong[Responding to Imām Mālik's Ḥadīth:] The ḥadīth cited by Imām
Mālik says #emph["whoever reaches Arafah at night has attained the
Hajj."] The Ḥanafī response: this ḥadīth affirms that the night is a
valid time, but it is #strong[silent] about the daytime --- it neither
validates nor rejects it. Silence cannot be used as evidence to negate
the validity of the daytime wuqūf.

#horizontalrule

== Point 4 --- Case of Mistaken Dates
<point-4-case-of-mistaken-dates>
=== Case: Wuqūf Performed on the 10th (Thinking it was the 9th)
<case-wuquf-performed-on-the-10th-thinking-it-was-the-9th>
If the people counted the month of Dhul Qaʿdah (the month before Dhul
Ḥijjah) as thirty days, performed the wuqūf on what they believed was
the 9th, but later witnesses testified that Dhul Qaʿdah was only
twenty-nine days --- meaning the wuqūf was actually performed on the
#strong[10th of Dhul Ḥijjah];:

#strong[Ruling:] The wuqūf is #strong[valid];. What is done is done. It
cannot be invalidated because: - It affects a large number of people,
not just one individual. - Their money and effort would go to waste. -
It happened due to a genuine mistake, which is forgiven.

The dalīl is the ḥadīth:

#quote(block: true)[
صَوْمُكُمْ يَوْمَ تَصُومُونَ وَأَضْحَاكُمْ يَوْمَ تُضَحُّونَ وَحَجُّكُمْ يَوْمَ تَحُجُّونَ

#emph["Your fasting is the day you fast, your sacrifice is the day you
sacrifice, and your Hajj is the day you perform it \[according to your
counting\]."]

#strong[(hadith as cited in class --- confirm in hadith index)]
]

=== Why the Testimony is Not Accepted to Invalidate
<why-the-testimony-is-not-accepted-to-invalidate>
+ The testimony of those witnesses is a #strong[shahādah for nafī]
  (testimony to negate), which is inherently weaker (badīlī). It seeks
  to invalidate the Hajj of the masses, and such negating testimony is
  not given precedence.
+ Even if the witnesses are trustworthy, accepting such testimony would
  create #strong[ḥaraj (حَرَج)] \[undue hardship\] for all the pilgrims.
  Such a mistake is a normal occurrence that cannot be avoided, so it is
  forgiven.

#horizontalrule

=== Case: Wuqūf Performed on the 8th (Thinking it was the 9th)
<case-wuquf-performed-on-the-8th-thinking-it-was-the-9th>
If the people counted the previous month as twenty-nine days and
performed the wuqūf on what they thought was the 9th, but it later
turned out to be only the #strong[8th of Dhul Ḥijjah];:

#strong[Ruling:] The wuqūf is #strong[not valid];. They must repeat it
on the actual 9th, because there is still time and opportunity to
perform it correctly. The necessity that would justify accepting a
premature wuqūf does not exist here --- the correct date is still ahead.

#strong[Key distinction:] - Wuqūf on the 10th (after the time has
passed) → valid, because there is no chance to repeat it. - Wuqūf on the
8th (before the time has arrived) → invalid, because the 9th is still to
come and the correct wuqūf can still be performed.

#horizontalrule

